{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789487354,"nonce":"dzNWRPKmVD4E/W7IKqMSZjAxzE4=","title":"Lowering copies the whole symbol table into every function's SSA builder","message":"`lower_function` built each function's `SsaBuilder` with clones of `symbols.functions`, `extern_link_names`, `function_default_params`, `function_return_types`, `function_param_types`, `fiber_fn_names` and `body_fn_names`: with the builtins library declared that is about 530 entries in each, the param and return types deep-cloned. Around 60 us per function before a line of the body was lowered; the prelude's 45 exception-class functions alone cost 4 ms of every run, an `X$unbox` of twenty instructions 91 us.\n\nNow the tables are `Arc`s shared with the builder, which only reads them; a writer in the lowerer takes `Arc::make_mut`, which copies nothing while no builder holds the table (a builder is consumed by its build). Measured on the M1 Pro under load: `lower_decls` on a trivial program 5.1 to 2.9 ms, `X$unbox` 91 to 37 us, the trivial program's compile 13.4 to 10.4 ms.\n\nLeft per function: the typed CFG and SSA construction proper, `module_globals()` rebuilt per function, and the per-parameter maps.","files":null}]}